course: dictionary
lesson: 1735
title: Clammy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clammy is an adjective, and it describes something that is unpleasantly damp, cold and sticky, especially skin. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «The air so clammy and chill, and not an insect in an acre of it!» The words chill and not an insect show the air is cold and damp, so clammy means damp and cold.
explain: Clammy can also describe weather. When it is clammy and warm, the air feels heavy and sticky, as if it is hard to breathe. Ask yourself what the word would feel like if you touched it, then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it fits.
explain: Writers use clammy to show feelings as well. A character with clammy hands is often scared or nervous, just before a test or a scary moment. The word tells the reader how the character feels without saying it outright.
fact: Clammy means unpleasantly damp, cold and sticky to touch, especially skin.
fact: Clammy can also describe weather: clammy air is damp, heavy, warm and sticky.
fact: In stories, «clammy hands» often show fear or nerves.
fact: Pale clammy skin can be a sign that someone is unwell or in shock, so always tell an adult.
fact: Heat exhaustion signs include headache, dizziness, feeling sick, being very thirsty, heavy sweating, pale clammy skin and cramps.
exercise: «The air so clammy and chill, and not an insect in an acre of it!» What does clammy mean here? | Dry and dusty | Hot and bright | *Damp and cold | Loud and buzzing
exercise: Sam's hands felt clammy before his spelling test. What is Sam probably feeling? | Very proud | Bored and sleepy | *Nervous | Thirsty for juice
exercise: Pale clammy skin, a headache and feeling sick can be signs of heat exhaustion. What should you do? | Eat a big bag of sweets | Ignore it and keep running | *Tell an adult straight away | Lie in the hot sun to warm up
test: In a steamy forest, the air felt clammy and heavy. What does clammy suggest about the air? | *Damp, heavy and warm | Crisp and fresh | Sparkling clear | Icy and thin
test: Why should you tell an adult if someone has pale clammy skin? | *Because they may be unwell or in shock | Because clammy means happy | Because adults like to hear about skin | Because clammy skin is always harmless
exam: Which sentence uses clammy to show fear or nerves? | *Lena wiped her clammy hands before she walked on stage | Lena ran across the field to catch the bus | Lena ate a cold ice lolly on the beach | Lena sang a happy song with her friends
